{"t":13.95,"agent":"legal","run":"run-2026-09-27T21-22-19-733","type":"answer","text":"Short answer: Not yet — one confirmation is still outstanding, so don't sign this week until that clears.\n\nWhat's verified:\n- Gripworks MSA v3 is fully negotiated: 12-month term, Net-45, 1x fees liability cap, $40k value, all redlines resolved (Sep 20).\n- Legal approved the MSA on Sep 22 (General Counsel Tomas Reyes), but that approval is explicitly logged as \"pending budget confirmation.\"\n- Signing authority: since the contract is over $30k, it requires the CEO (Mara Okafor) or COO (Dev Lindqvist) to sign — not the GC alone.\n- Gripworks itself passed vendor risk review in August and was selected after the Gripper v2 bake-off.\n\nThe gap: Finance's confirmation that the $40k is actually covered by Q4 supplier-line budget headroom has not come back yet — I've sent that question to the finance team and don't have their answer in hand. I did not invent a budget status.\n\nBottom line: legally the contract is ready and approved pending that one condition. To sign this week, get Finance's budget confirmation and then route it to Mara Okafor or Dev Lindqvist for signature — everything else is clear.","citations":["companies/gripworks","legal/gripworks-msa","legal/approvals","people/signatories"],"blocked":true}
